title: "SputterOne: A Physics-Informed Reduced-Order Magnetron Sputtering Simulation Platform"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2025-01-01
url: "https://balaji-gururajan90.github.io/SputterOne/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/balaji-gururajan90/SputterOne"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - magnetron sputtering
  - reduced-order modelling
  - physics-informed simulation
  - thin-film deposition
  - process optimisation
  - browser-based simulator
abstract: "SputterOne is a browser-based physics-informed reduced-order simulation platform 
for real-time exploration of magnetron sputtering process conditions. It integrates the 
Yamamura-Bohdansky sputtering yield formulation, kinetic-theory mean free path transport, 
probabilistic gas-phase scattering, Berg-framework reactive sputtering hysteresis, 
co-sputtering composition estimation, and Bauer-scheme growth mode classification."
